      "solution": "g=input().strip()\nk=int(input())\nres=[]\nfor _ in range(k):\n    a,b=map(int,input().split())\n    if g=='BUFFER': r=a\n    elif g=='NOT': r=1-a\n    elif g=='AND': r=a&b\n    elif g=='OR': r=a|b\n    elif g=='NAND': r=1-(a&b)\n    elif g=='NOR': r=1-(a|b)\n    elif g=='XOR': r=a^b\n    else: r=1-(a^b)\n    res.append(str(r))\nprint(' '.join(res))",
      "statement": "A logic gate takes binary inputs (0 or 1) and produces a binary output.\nYou are given a gate name and several pairs of input values.\nFor each pair, evaluate the gate and print the resulting bit.\nAll answers must be printed on a single line, space-separated.\n\nSupported gates:\nBUFFER: output = input A (0 becomes 0, 1 becomes 1)\nNOT: output = 1 - A\nAND: output = 1 only if A = 1 and B = 1, otherwise 0\nOR: output = 1 if at least one of A, B is 1, otherwise 0\nNAND: opposite of AND\nNOR: opposite of OR\nXOR: output = 1 if A and B differ, otherwise 0\nXNOR: opposite of XOR\n\nFor BUFFER and NOT, the second value on a line is ignored.",
